I walk straight ahead along the harbour.
I walk past the small boats.
Suddenly I see many people.
They stand down by the water.
I walk over there.
Finally, I see it.
The Little Mermaid sits on a stone out in the water.
She is a very famous statue in Copenhagen.
The figure is actually not very big.
But the bronze figure is beautiful in the sun.
I stand among the other visitors.
Many tourists take pictures of the statue.
I also take out my phone.
I take a beautiful picture of the mermaid.
I send the picture to my family in Mexico.
My sister, Sofía, answers quickly.
"She is very pretty," she writes.
I look at the water again.
